# at_rest.scene
# Tests that a mixed collection of balls and boxes come to rest in the natural
# terrain bowl. No water — buoyancy keeps objects gently afloat near the surface
# and prevents them from fully settling, which defeats the purpose of this test.
#
# Objects are scattered above the center of the bowl and dropped under gravity.
# The scene runs for 1800 frames (~30s at 60Hz) to give everything time to settle.
# All objects should reach sleep state before the scene ends.
#
# Useful for eyeballing contact-resting quality. See Bugs.md for known issues
# with ball-on-terrain contact resting state.

physics on
text on
frames 1800
fixed_step
time_scale 10.0
physics_mode solver
world -9.81 0.0 0.0
water_hidden on

# Overview camera looking down into the bowl
camera overview  340 200 430  520 30 540  0 1 0

# --- Balls ---
# ball <name> <posX> <posY> <posZ> <radius> <mass> <moment> <restitution>
ball ball_a  490 110 490  8.0 30.0 15.0 0.4
ball ball_b  550 120 515  7.0 24.0 12.0 0.35
ball ball_c  505 100 555  9.0 36.0 18.0 0.3

# --- Boxes ---
# box <name> <posX> <posY> <posZ> <halfX> <halfY> <halfZ> <mass> <restitution> [eulerX eulerY eulerZ]
box box_a  525 90 490  3.0 3.0 3.0  22.0 0.3
box box_b  475 105 540  4.0 2.5 3.0  30.0 0.25  0 20 0
box box_c  545 100 545  2.5 3.5 2.5  18.0 0.3  15 0 25
